From: Linux psX contributors
Subject: [PATCH] radv: disable HTILE on Liverpool pending metadata qualification

On the tested Liverpool/Baikal B1 stack, a 64x64 D16 depth test completes
with RADV_DEBUG=nohiz and verifies all 4096 expected pixels. The identical
test with HTILE enabled allocates depth metadata, submits successfully,
then times out. Graphics fences remain outstanding; no UVD commands were
submitted. EXP-20261021-001/002 isolate the HTILE-enabled path as a trigger,
but do not establish the underlying metadata addressing or clear defect.

Disable HiZ/HTILE policy for Liverpool. Ordinary depth testing remains
available, at the cost of depth compression/HiZ optimization. Set the policy
before feature/property initialization so image allocation and advertised
compression properties agree. Preserve the existing debug override and
all other families, including Gladius.

This is a conservative workaround motivated by one tested console, not a
claim of full Vulkan conformance or hardware acceptance for other devices.

License: MIT; existing per-file notices remain unchanged.

---
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
@@ -2698,7 +2698,11 @@
 
    pdev->force_64_byte_sampled_image = !pdev->use_fmask && instance->drirc.debug.force_64_byte_sampled_image;
 
-   pdev->use_hiz = !(instance->debug_flags & RADV_DEBUG_NO_HIZ);
+   /* Liverpool depth draws can hang with HTILE enabled. Keep ordinary depth
+    * testing available while the metadata path is unqualified.
+    */
+   pdev->use_hiz = pdev->info.family != CHIP_LIVERPOOL &&
+                   !(instance->debug_flags & RADV_DEBUG_NO_HIZ);
 
    if (pdev->info.gfx_level == GFX12) {
       const char *gfx12_hiz_wa_str = instance->drirc.performance.gfx12_hiz_wa;
